# package.provided — packages portage treats as pre-installed without building.
#
# Cross-compile exclusions: these packages require the aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu
# Rust stdlib target on the host (not present in the system dev-lang/rust build).
# They provide SVG rendering / icon themes — irrelevant on a minimal LXDE SBC
# (hicolor PNG fallback icons are sufficient). Listing them here satisfies any
# DEPEND/RDEPEND without portage attempting to emerge them into the sysroot.
#
# gtk+'s own librsvg dep is removed via package.use (-rsvg); the entries below
# satisfy gtk+'s adwaita RDEPEND and any other packages that pull adwaita/librsvg.
#
# IMPORTANT: update these version numbers if the portage tree upgrades the atoms —
# the versions must be ≥ whatever version satisfies the dependency constraint.
gnome-base/librsvg-2.62.2-r1
x11-themes/adwaita-icon-theme-49.0
x11-themes/adwaita-icon-theme-legacy-46.2

# www-client/netsurf cross-compile fails: netsurf's duktape JS binding generator
# requires net-libs/nsgenbind as a native BUILD tool, but nsgenbind is not installed
# on the cross-compile host (only x86_64 and i686 Rust/toolchain targets are present).
# Listing netsurf as provided satisfies any dep that references it; the browser can be
# installed post-first-boot via native aarch64 emerge on the target hardware.
www-client/netsurf-3.11-r1

# dev-perl/JSON-XS cross-compile fails: Perl XS modules compile native C using the
# host's Perl ExtUtils::MakeMaker config, but the resulting object targets aarch64
# (CHOST) — the linker step fails because the host Perl ABI != target. JSON-XS is
# an optional fast-path for dev-perl/JSON; the pure-Perl fallback is sufficient.
dev-perl/JSON-XS-4.40.0
